Description: Linux daemon for the ASUS ZenBook Duo 2024 (UX8406MA)
 zbd fills the gap between the upstream kernel/desktop stack and the
 ASUS ZenBook Duo 2024 — a laptop with two stacked OLED panels and a
 detachable Bluetooth/USB keyboard. It detects the keyboard
 transition (attached vs detached), enables or disables the second
 internal display (eDP-2) accordingly, sets per-output wallpapers via
 gsettings, drives the keyboard backlight via the vendor HID protocol,
 caps the battery charge and wires the Intel Smart Sound DMIC into the
 default PulseAudio source.
 .
 Two binaries are installed:
   * /usr/sbin/zbd-system — hardened, sandboxed systemd service that
     applies the persistent hardware tunables (backlight, battery,
     keyboard backlight, DMIC) at boot and exposes them over D-Bus
     (org.anexa.zbd1) with polkit authorisation.
   * /usr/bin/zbd-tray   — GLib tray (no GTK) + event monitors
     (Bluetooth, USB hotplug, iio-sensor-proxy) running in the user's
     graphical session.
 .
 The display backend is selected at runtime: gdctl on Wayland/GNOME
 (default on Ubuntu 26.04), xrandr on X11.  Wallpapers are set via
 gsettings in both cases; feh and XWayland are not required.
